---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from "../site.ts";

// Keep this page accurate to the code. Update it whenever analytics, hosting or features change.
const updated = "2026-10-26";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy – ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description="Your GCash statement is processed on your device and never uploaded. Read exactly what this site does and doesn't collect."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">
      Last updated <time datetime={updated}>October 26, 2026</time>
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Your GCash statement, its password and your transactions never leave your device. The
      converter runs entirely in your web browser. We don't have a server that could receive your
      file, and we don't want one.
    </p>

    <h2>Your statement and password</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        When you choose a PDF, your browser reads it locally. It is not uploaded, emailed, logged or
        sent to analytics.
      </li>
      <li>
        The password you type is used only to open the PDF on your device. It isn't saved in your
        browser, in cookies or in the page address, and the password box is cleared after
        converting.
      </li>
      <li>
        The Excel and CSV files are created on your device and saved straight to it by your browser.
      </li>
      <li>
        Everything is kept in memory only while the page is open. Closing or refreshing the page
        clears it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What this website collects</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>No accounts, no cookies, no advertising trackers.</strong>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting logs.</strong> The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host,
        Cloudflare processes basic technical data needed to deliver pages and protect the site, such
        as your IP address and browser type. This never includes your statement or password. See{" "}
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics.</strong> We don't currently use analytics. If we add it, we will only use
        privacy-friendly, cookieless page-view counts (such as Cloudflare Web Analytics) and update
        this page first. Statement data will never be included.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How you can check</h2>
    <p>
      Open your browser's developer tools, go to the Network tab and convert a statement. You'll see
      the site load its own files, and no request that sends your PDF or its contents anywhere. The
      site's security settings also block the page from contacting other servers.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not directed at children and doesn't knowingly collect anyone's personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
